Critical Script Runtime Readiness Audit
Maximum Report Length: 5–7 Pages

Perform a focused, project-wide audit of the complete current script to determine whether everything required for the project to load, initialize, and execute is present and correctly connected.

Review all current script files and modules together as one executable project.

Treat the current source code as authoritative. Completed audit reports may be used as supporting references, but independently verify all potentially blocking findings against the current code.

Hard Output Limit

The final report must:

Be no longer than 7 pages
Target approximately 5–7 pages
Not exceed 3,500 words
Contain no appendices
Contain no separate cross-reference reports
Contain no complete function inventory
Contain no complete call graph
Contain no separate execution trace for every passing menu item or trigger
Contain no repeated descriptions of shared functions, helpers, wrappers, or constants

Audit the complete project, but report detailed information only for:

Critical failures
High-risk failures
Missing components
Broken connections
Conflicting definitions
Unresolved dependencies
Conditions that could halt or corrupt execution
Items that cannot be verified

Summarize passing components using totals and status counts.

AUDIT OBJECTIVE

Verify that nothing required for execution is missing, inaccessible, conflicting, or incorrectly connected, including:

Script files and modules
Menu registration
Trigger registration
Callbacks
Functions
Wrappers
Helpers
Validators
Global definitions
Constants
Configuration objects
Object properties
Script properties
Worksheet definitions
Template definitions
Required resources
Google Apps Script services
Initialization order
Error and cleanup handling

Focus only on issues that could:

Prevent the script from loading
Prevent menus from opening
Prevent triggers from firing
Prevent callbacks from resolving
Stop a workflow
Cause an undefined reference
Cause invalid initialization
Cause a required resource to be unavailable
Cause partial or corrupt processing
Leave locks or runtime state unresolved
SECTION 1 — PROJECT LOAD READINESS

Verify:

Every required production module is present.
No required source file is empty or truncated.
No unresolved merge markers remain.
No syntax error prevents parsing.
No malformed function, object, array, comment, or string remains.
No duplicate global definition creates a conflict.
No required project or manifest file is missing.
Modular and combined files do not omit required components.

Report only failures and warnings.

